# Document-sandbox served assets. The two bundles are esbuild output committed so
# the reviewed bytes are the served bytes; a drift test asserts they equal a fresh
# build, so reformatting them would break that byte-equality. The pyodide runtime
# is fetched, pinned third-party wasm/wheels.
apps/sandbox/public/render.js
apps/sandbox/public/python.js
apps/sandbox/public/pyodide/

# The marketing site, built a second time and copied into the admin origin's
# static assets, where that origin's bundler carries it into the dist its assets
# Worker serves. Everything under it is that build's output, held to that
# build's rules, so formatting any of it would rewrite what it produced. The
# directory is named here rather than left to the ignore file beside the copy:
# this tool reads the repository's root ignore file and not a nested one.
apps/admin/public/preview/

# Captured upstream package-registry responses, replayed verbatim in tests.
# Reformatting them would change the bytes under replay.
apps/sandbox/test-fixtures/

# Audit findings, their skeletons, and the parser's fixtures. The format quotes
# every frontmatter string with JSON escaping and reads it back with
# `JSON.parse`, so `singleQuote: true` would rewrite `id: "AI-1"` to `id: 'AI-1'`
# and make every finding unparseable. Reformatting would also break the
# byte-identical round trip that keeps a no-op write from touching the file.
# `docs/audits/CLAUDE.md` is prose, not format, and stays formatted.
docs/audits/*/
.claude/skills/improve-codebase/template/audit.md
.claude/skills/improve-codebase/template/finding.md
packages/docket/test-fixtures/

# Run records: a plan, a ledger and the task reports, written during a run and
# never updated afterwards (`docs/CODE-RULES.md` §Doc Lifecycle). Formatting them
# would rewrite a historical record.
docs/runs/

# The billing behaviour ledger. One row per line is load-bearing: a behaviour's whole
# entry is a single line, so a review diff reads as one line per behaviour changed and a
# row can be edited without navigating a block. `pnpm format` is a documented command
# (`docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`), and reformatting would explode each row across ~20 lines,
# destroying that shape.
packages/config/behaviour-ledger.json

# The frontend-design skill's two vendored halves: the craft guides under
# `reference/` and the detector under `scripts/`, both seeded verbatim at a
# pinned commit from `pbakaus/impeccable` (Apache-2.0) and since maintained
# here as a fork, so the two directories hold that vendored code plus HushBox
# additions written in its style — this exempts both. Dev-only tooling that
# ships to no user and runs on no production path; none of it was written to
# this repo's conventions, and it is deliberately not held to them. The
# provenance, the fork's divergence, and the three further upstreams the skill
# merges are recorded in `.claude/skills/frontend-design/.MAINTAINERS.md`.
# Scoped to those two directories, so HushBox-authored files outside them —
# the skill's own, and first-party code elsewhere under `.claude/` — stay
# formatted.
.claude/skills/frontend-design/reference/
.claude/skills/frontend-design/scripts/

